Legal text

Laws, regulations, resolutions, decisions and orders of state organs and their official translations are not
protected by copyright in the People's Republic of China (中华人民共和国著作权法第五条). The texts here come from
中国人大网 (www.npc.gov.cn). Source: 中国人大网, https://www.npc.gov.cn/.

The 中国人大网 site publishes no reuse terms for this section that we could find; this repository stays private
until reuse is confirmed.

The Constitution, the codes and the laws in this repository (xianfa/, xingfa/, xingshisusongfa/, gongsifa/,
laodonghetongfa/ and any act folder added later) are laws and decisions of the National People's Congress and its
Standing Committee, which the Copyright Law of the People's Republic of China excludes from its protection:

    中华人民共和国著作权法（2020年修正）第五条：“本法不适用于：（一）法律、法规，国家机关的决议、决定、命令和其他具有立法、行政、司法性质的文件，及其官方正式译文；（二）单纯事实消息；（三）历法、通用数表、通用表格和公式。”

    ("This Law does not apply to: (1) laws and regulations, resolutions, decisions and orders of state organs, and other
    documents of a legislative, administrative or judicial nature, and their official translations; (2) mere news of
    facts; (3) calendars, general numerical tables, general tables and formulas.")

